s="\"ISSN 1855-3966 (printed edn.), ISSN 1855-3974 (electronic edn.) (https://www.dlib.si/stream/URN%3ANBN%3ASI%3ADOC-05TQJS6H/0b433388-ece2-4e0e-b676-beb051f82b80/PDF)\\nciteturn0search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; This paper deals with some algebraic properties of Sierpi´nski graphs and a family of ... Keywords: Sierpi´nski graph, spectrum, Laplacian, Cayley graph, non-Cayley number.\\nISSN 1855-3966 (printed edn.), ISSN 1855-3974 (electronic edn.)\\nARS MATHEMATICA CONTEMPORANEA 20 (2021) 171–186\\nhttps://doi.org/10.26493/1855-3974.2199.97e\\n(Also available at http://amc-journal.eu)\\nSome algebraic properties of\\nSierpi´nski-type graphs*\\nMohammad Farrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan\\nDepartment of Mathematics, Institute for Advanced Studies in Basic Sciences (IASBS),\\nand the Center for Research in Basic Sciences and Contemporary Technologies, IASBS,\\nP. O. Box 45137-66731, Zanjan, Iran\\nEbrahim Ghorbani †\\nDepartment of Mathematics, K. N. Toosi University of Technology,\\nP. O. Box 16765-3381, Tehran, Iran\\nHamid Reza Maimani\\n, Farhad Rahimi Mahid\\nDepartment of Basic Sciences, Shahid Rajaee Teacher Training University,\\nP. O. Box 16783-163, Tehran, Iran\\nReceived 16 December 2019, accepted 4 November 2020, published online 21 October 2021\\nAbstract\\nThis paper deals with some algebraic properties of Sierpi´nski graphs and a family of\\nregular generalized Sierpi´nski graphs. For the family of regular generalized Sierpi´nski\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSome Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.04037)\\nciteturn0academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.2 years ago; Title: Some Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs ... This paper deals with some of the algebraic properties of Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs and a family of regular generalized Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs.\\nTitle: Some Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs\\nAuthors: Mohammad Farrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan, E. Ghorbani, H. R. Maimani, F. Rahimi Mahid\\nDate: Mon Aug 12 07:38:44 2019\\n\\nThis paper deals with some of the algebraic properties of Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs and a family of regular generalized Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs. For the family of regular generalized Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs, we obtain their spectrum and characterize those graphs that are Cayley graphs. As a by-product, a new family of non-Cayley vertex-transitive graphs, and consequently, a new set of non-Cayley numbers are introduced. We also obtain the Laplacian spectrum of Sierpi\\\\'nski graphs in some particular cases, and make a conjecture on the general case.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nJ. Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21 (https://scispace.com/pdf/the-sierpinski-product-of-graphs-1r0hy4x9.pdf)\\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.2 years ago; Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21 ... Then the group* Â(G, G, f) *is a semidirect product,* ... By Proposition 3.23, every element of Â(G, G, f) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f).\\nJ. Kovič et al.: The Sierpiński product of graphs 21\\n\\n**Proposition 3.24.** *Let G be a connected graph and let f : V(G) → V(G) be an automorphism. Then the group* B̂(G, G, f) *is a normal subgroup of the group* Â(G, G, f).\\n\\n*Proof.* Observe that the function λ : Â(G, G, f) → Â(G, f) defined by λ : Ψ(α, β) → Ψ(α, f ◦ α ◦ f⁻¹) is a homomorphism of groups, with B̂(G, G, f) being its kernel. Therefore, B̂(G, G, f) is a normal subgroup of Â(G, G, f).\\n\\n**Theorem 3.25.** *Let G be a connected graph and let f : V(G) → V(G) be an automorphism. Then the group* Â(G, G, f) *is a semidirect product,*\\n\\nÂ(G, G, f) = Â(G, f) × B̂(G, G, f).\\n\\n*Proof.* The group B̂(G, G, f) is a normal subgroup of Â(G, G, f) by Proposition 3.24. By Proposition 3.23, every element of Â(G, G, f) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f). Moreover, only the identity is in both Â(G, f) and B̂(G, G, f). This proves that Â(G, G, f) is a semidirect product of Â(G, f) and B̂(G, G, f).\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndLib.si - Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs (https://www.dlib.si/details/URN%3ANBN%3ASI%3Adoc-05TQJS6H)\\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.0 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; # Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs\\n\\n# Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs\\n\\nImage: tab1\\n\\n1. PDF datoteka (431 kB)\\n\\n1. TXT datoteka (43 kB)\\n\\n   Izvoz v EndNote (RIS format)\\n\\nAvtor(ji)\\n\\nFarrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan,, Mohammad (avtor)\\nGhorbani, Ebrahim (avtor)\\nMaimani, Hamid Reza (avtor)\\nMahid, Farhad Rahimi (avtor)\\n\\nJezik\\n\\nangleški\\n\\nVir\\n\\nArs mathematica contemporanea\\n\\nLeto\\n\\n2021\\n\\nŠtevilčenje\\n\\nletnik 20, številka 2\\n\\nVsebina\\n\\nCayleyjev graf   graf Sierpińskega   Laplaceov operator   ne-Cayleyjevo število   spekter\\n\\nZaložnik\\n\\nUniverza na Primorskem, Fakulteta za matematiko, naravoslovje in informacijske tehnologije\\n\\nIzvor\\n\\nUniverza na Primorskem, Fakulteta za naravoslovje, matematiko in informacijske tehnologije\\n(Obvezni izvod spletne publikacije)\\n\\nOpis\\n\\nV članku obravnavamo nekaj algebrajskih lastnosti grafov Sierpińskega in družino regularnih posplošenih grafov Sierpińskega. Za družino regularnih posplošenih grafov Sierpińskega določimo njihov spekter in karakteriziramo tiste grafe, ki so Cayleyjevi grafi. Poleg tega vpeljemo novo družino ne-Cayleyjevih vozliščno tranzitivnih grafov in, temu ustrezno, novo množico ne-Cayleyjevih števil. Določimo tudi Laplaceov spekter grafov Sierpińskega v nekaj posebnih primerih, postavimo pa tudi hipotezo v zvezi s splošnim primerom.\\n\\n\\nURN\\n\\nURN:NBN:SI:doc-05TQJS6H\\n\\nCOBISSID\\n\\n91633411\\n\\nDOI\\n\\n10.26493/1855-3974.2199.97e\\n\\nObjavljeno\\n\\n22.11.2022\\n\\nMetapodatki\\n\\nCitiranje\\n\\nAPA:\\n\\nFarrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan,, Mohammad, Ghorbani, Ebrahim, Maimani, Hamid Reza, Mahid, Farhad Rahimi (2021). Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs. Ars mathematica contemporanea, letnik 20, številka 2, str. 171-186. URN:NBN:SI:doc-05TQJS6H from http://www.dlib.si\\n\\nMLA:\\n\\nFarrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan,, Mohammad, Ghorbani, Ebrahim, Maimani, Hamid Reza, Mahid, Farhad Rahimi. \\\"Some algebraic properties of Sierpiński-type graphs.\\\" Ars mathematica contemporanea letnik 20. številka 2 (2021) str. 171-186.\\n<http://www.dlib.si/?URN=URN:NBN:SI:doc-05TQJS6H>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nThe Sierpi\\\\'nski product of graphs (https://www.academia.edu/178902227/The_Sierpi_nski_product_of_graphs)\\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Then the group Ã(G, G, f ) is a semidirect product, Ã(G, G, f ) = Ā(G, f ) ⋉ B̂(G, G, f ). ... By Theorem 3.25, every element of Ã(G, G, f ) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f ). ... 4 Sierpiński product with multiple factors When extending the Sierpiński product to more than two factors we first need to specify how the graph G embeds into the product G ⊗f H in order to be able to multiply it with the next graph.\\n Theorem 3.27. Let G be a connected graph and let f : V (G) → V (G) be an automorphism. Then the group Ã(G, G, f ) is a semidirect product, Ã(G, G, f ) = Ā(G, f ) ⋉ B̂(G, G, f ). Proof. Group B̂(G, G, f ) is a normal subgroup of Ã(G, G, f ) by Theorem 3.26. By Theorem 3.25, every element of Ã(G, G, f ) can be written as a product of a diagonal automorphism and an element from B̂(G, G, f ). Moreover, only identity is in both Ā(G, f ) and B̂(G, G, f ). This proves that Ã(G, G, f ) is a semidirect product of Ā(G, f ) and B̂(G, G, f ). Note that in general not every automorphism of G has a lift. Diagonal mappings are well defined only if f is a bijection. Define Ā(G, H, f ) to be the set of all diagonal mappings that are also automorphisms. This is a subgroup of Ã(G, H, f ). We believe that the following conjecture holds. 16 Conjecture 3.28. Let G and H be connected graphs on the same vertex set and let f : V (G) → V (H) be a bijection. Then the group Ã(G, H, f ) is a semidirect product, Ã(G, H, f ) = Ā(G, H, f ) ⋉ B̂(G, H, f ). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSome Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs - arXiv Combinatorics (https://www.arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/1908.04037v4)\\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.2 years ago; Crawled: last week; ## Some Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs ... This paper deals with some of the algebraic properties of Sierpiński graphs and a family of regular generalized Sierpiński graphs.\\n\\n## Some Algebraic Properties of Sierpiński-Type Graphs\\n\\nMohammad Farrokhi Derakhshandeh Ghouchan, E. Ghorbani, H. R. Maimani, F. Rahimi Mahid\\n\\nPublished: 2019-08-12 | Updated: 2020-11-10\\n\\nComments: 16 pages, final version\\n\\nDOI: 10.26493/1855-3974.2199.97e\\n\\ngraph vertex-transitive graph\\n\\n# • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\\n\\n### Abstract\\n\\nThis paper deals with some of the algebraic properties of Sierpiński graphs and a family of regular generalized Sierpiński graphs. For the family of regular generalized Sierpiński graphs, we obtain their spectrum and characterize those graphs that are Cayley graphs. As a by-product, a new family of non-Cayley vertex-transitive graphs, and consequently, a new set of non-Cayley numbers are introduced. We also obtain the Laplacian spectrum of Sierpiński graphs in some particular cases, and make a conjecture on the general case.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSimpConn5.dv